  "fixture": "Checkpoint Atlas",
  "method": {
    "store": "Every game opens the existing createSaveStore from @egret/engine/kit, using services.storage and the same key, progress. Both asset roots carry byte-identical game bundles and game names. No browser localStorage or direct native seeding is used.",
    "continuity": "One signed QA application, package and signing certificate shared by all three hosts. Android replaces the APK with install -r while retaining app data. The runner validates the installed APK SHA-256, runs am force-stop for the current user, and observes the process absent and the package stopped. Each recovery from an active game additionally verifies a different PID and Android COLD launch classification. Preparatory stop commands against an already absent process are counted separately.",
    "production": "final-v1 and final-v2 use the same production AAR for each host. Application versionCode and authored save schema advance from 1 to 2. Each host seeds an extra game root under v1 so the corresponding host really migrates a v1 value under v2 and observes a v2 read with zero migrations on the following cold launch. The shared A and B roots additionally carry progress across all three host APKs.",
    "data": "At each checkpoint the fixture rebuilds the expected complete data, checks both in-memory and stored envelopes, and reports load version and migration count. The test separately reads the app-private installed file as its owner and verifies the complete expected JSON data, timestamp shape, encoded byte count and SHA-256. The UTF-8 boundary uses a separate key and contains both a Chinese character and an emoji.",
    "gate": "The separate diag-single APK uses its diagnostic AAR with private observation calls around atomic rename, after the temporary file has been forced. It holds only an explicitly armed large write. The test reads the old published and complete staged envelopes from the app sandbox. One run force-stops while staged. The next calls the real EgretPlayerView.close, observes onClosed pending, releases the writer and verifies the atomic move precedes onClosed. The game only records the synchronous save result in a local variable; closedSnapshot then returns that value. Stock AARs contain no gate. Millisecond values reflect artificial gate ordering.",
    "scope": "Observed application-process force-stop and view close/reopen on one Fold7. These trials do not exercise device power loss, backup, cloud synchronization or cross-application storage."
  },
